      "created_at": "2022-05-30T12:57:34Z",
      "updated_at": "2022-05-30T12:57:34Z",
      "body": "> It might be okay to tell a user that \"some other user is already using this destination address\", but that should still not prevent a user from doing so.\r\n\r\nAlthough, this could still be a breach of privacy. If you want to know if John Doe is a user of the system, and you know their e-mail is john.doe@example.org, you could attempt to add that address and be told in clear text that \"yes, John Doe probably has an account here\" (of course, this scenario could be a bit far fetched in an enterprise setting anyway).\r\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
